  "question": {
    "text": "An electron revolving in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mtext>th </mtext></msup></math> Bohr orbit has magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>∝</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math>, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is:",
    "image": null
  },
